        "id": 11435,
        "name": "seesome",
        "username": "seesome",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-20T17:01:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<div><div><span>If one player MUST redirect all damage to themselves (e.g. Scholar with Alchemical Redirection), while another MAY redirect any damage to themselves (e.g. Stealth Bot), do we still have the choice of the order of events? &nbsp;That is, could we either have Scholar take the damage and then redirect it to Stealth Bot at a minus 1 OR have Stealth Bot take the damage and reduce it by 1 and then redirect it to Scholar.</span></div></div><div>&nbsp;</div><div>I believe I saw here that the reduction only happens once, so no infinite looping of redirect to eliminate the damage (which makes sense), but I wanted to confirm that \"MAY\" vs \"MUST\" didn't override the player choice of determining the sequence of events.</div>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:44.557Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
