        "raw": "<p>With the wording what would happen is Scholar and Stealth Bot would both be able to redirect the damage to themselves at the same time. &nbsp;So the Players would choose which one to redirect to.</p><p>If the Players choose to resolve Scholar first they then have the option to redirect to Stealth Bot.</p><p>If the Players choose to resolve Stealth Bot and redirect it, Scholar will then redirect it to himself.</p><p>Each time Scholar would be dealt damage players have the opportunity to redirect it to Stealth Bot.</p><p>Each time Stealth Bot would be dealt damage Scholar will redirect it back to himself.</p><p>The result is an infinite loop that lasts exactly as long as you decide to have it last, before you let Scholar deal with the damage.</p><p>The reduction on Stealth Bot works as a simple yes/no question:</p><p>Was the damage redirected by Stealth Bot&#39;s effect? &nbsp;If so reduce that damage by 1. &nbsp;No multiple lowerings, and the effect doesn&#39;t expire from being redirected again.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If you have multiple &quot;Must&quot; redirections competing for the damage players choose which one ends up with the damage. &nbsp;(this is an obvious compromise to ending games in infinite loops)</p>",
